## 📝 Description

This PR includes a refactoring of `css-var.ts`, adds a helper function for creating and calculating css vars.

## 🚀 New behavior

The creation of css vars for a theme follows this pseudo code:

```ts
function createThemeVars(theme) {
  const tokens = extractTokens(theme)
  const cssVars = {}
  const cssMap = {}

  walkObject(tokens, (value, path) => {
    const key = path.join("-")
    cssVars[key] = value
  })

  return { cssVars, cssMap }
}
```

Create CSS vars:

```ts
const sliderWidth = cssVar("slider-width", "<fallback value>")
const { var, varRef } = sliderWidth
// var = --slider-width
// varRef = var(--slider-width, <fallback value>)
```

And calc CSS vars:

```ts
const translateX = calc.subtract(width, height).multiply(-1).toString()
```

## 💣 Is this a breaking change (Yes/No):

No

## 📝 Additional Information

Setting the move constructor and move assignment operator to = default
causes linker errors because the copy assignment operator is not
implemented in the TIterator base class.

Having the RooLinkedListIter move constructor and assignment operators
work is important to keep user code compatibility.

This is done to avoid breaking user code in the upcoming release (doesn't affect ROOT 6.24 because problem exists only since https://github.com/root-project/root/pull/7641).

With the current master, the linker error can be reproduces like this;
```C++
void iterator_test() {

    RooArgSet argSet1;
    RooArgSet argSet2;

    RooLinkedListIter iter{argSet1.iterator()};

    iter = argSet2.iterator();
}
```

